(3655940, 509485, 5885, '<td valign="top">Bravo dude. You got good camera skills and it''s paying off for ya. :-D</td>', 'Bravo dude. You got good camera skills and it''s paying off for ya. :-D', '2007-05-16 12:59:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(3656101, 508415, 4162, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the critique club:)<br/> <br/>I have lots of good things to say about this-I really liked it during voting and gave it an 8.<br/> <br/>Firstly it hits the challenge spot on (no pun intended)It portrays an interesting cultural event. The main character of the picture has a great look of concentration and the angle that you have taken this shows this off well, with most of his face showing.<br/> <br/>Use of Dof is great, focus is spot on on the main guy and the hand in the left corner is out of focus and so doesn''t attract attention. The background is nice and blurry...<br/> <br/>I think that the composition is great and you have caught the moment perfectly.  Colours and contrast are very natural looking-perhaps the blue could be a bit bluer...but that is just nit-picking!  <br/> <br/>I think that this is an excellent shot and I really have no ways to improve it! It would be interesting to see a shot of the man on his own too-of course this depends on the opportunities of the day.. Congrats on a new PB!  Natasha</td>', 'Greetings from the critique club:) I have lots of good things to say about this-I really liked it during voting and gave it an 8. Firstly it hits the challenge spot on (no pun intended)It portrays an interesting cultural event. The main character of the picture has a great look of concentration and the angle that you have taken this shows this off well, with most of his face showing. Use of Dof is great, focus is spot on on the main guy and the hand in the left corner is out of focus and so doesn''t attract attention. The background is nice and blurry... I think that the composition is great and you have caught the moment perfectly.  Colours and contrast are very natural looking-perhaps the blue could be a bit bluer...but that is just nit-picking!   I think that this is an excellent shot and I really have no ways to improve it! It would be interesting to see a shot of the man on his own too-of course this depends on the opportunities of the day.. Congrats on a new PB!  Natasha', '2007-05-16 13:36:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3656117, 508914, 42013, '<td valign="top">Hi from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/>Well, just out of the top 5 so it seems like you did something right! :)<br/> <br/>Your picture is striking. I particularly like the orange color of the background as it sets off the stitching of his hat quite nicely. You have given the viewer a couple of strong lines to peruse, particularly the leading lines of the fiddle''s neck up to the bow.<br/> <br/>By hiding most of the models face, the attention is placed more heavily on his hat and instrument. This gives it more of an impersonal feel but still gives a good sense of the holiday.<br/> <br/>Technicals are good, really my only nitpic is the mass of dark/shadow on the models right side(camera left). I suppose a small directional light coming from camera left could have given a little more depth the the shadows.<br/> <br/>PM me if you have any questions and good luck in your future challenges.<br/> <br/>Mark<br/> <br/></td>', 'Hi from the Critique Club, Well, just out of the top 5 so it seems like you did something right! :) Your picture is striking. I particularly like the orange color of the background as it sets off the stitching of his hat quite nicely. You have given the viewer a couple of strong lines to peruse, particularly the leading lines of the fiddle''s neck up to the bow. By hiding most of the models face, the attention is placed more heavily on his hat and instrument. This gives it more of an impersonal feel but still gives a good sense of the holiday. Technicals are good, really my only nitpic is the mass of dark/shadow on the models right side(camera left). I suppose a small directional light coming from camera left could have given a little more depth the the shadows. PM me if you have any questions and good luck in your future challenges. Mark ', '2007-05-16 13:42:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(3656185, 509369, 70171, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone for comments and support! :)<br/> <br/>i''ve made very little post processing. Just converted from raw and a little bit of crop to avoid CA of the lens on the border + usm + canvans + resize. It was a PELENG 8mm. This lens is like a trip in the photographic stone age(but it is new and produced in Byelorussia)! no autofocus: everything is manual and made in full metal, no plastic parts! but its effect is amazing.. pure fun :D a kiss to my boyfriend that has bought it :*<br/> <br/>it was a shame that this was in basic editing, i really was tempted to remove those crane in the background.. but doesn''t matter.. it is already a joy to arrive third!<br/> <br/>thanks everybody for comments and votes!<br/> <br/>p.s.: <a href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gino_De_Dominicis" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">HERE</a> some info about the giants and the artist that have create it.</td>', 'Thanks to everyone for comments and support! :) i''ve made very little post processing. Just converted from raw and a little bit of crop to avoid CA of the lens on the border + usm + canvans + resize. It was a PELENG 8mm. This lens is like a trip in the photographic stone age(but it is new and produced in Byelorussia)! no autofocus: everything is manual and made in full metal, no plastic parts! but its effect is amazing.. pure fun :D a kiss to my boyfriend that has bought it :* it was a shame that this was in basic editing, i really was tempted to remove those crane in the background.. but doesn''t matter.. it is already a joy to arrive third! thanks everybody for comments and votes! p.s.: HERE some info about the giants and the artist that have create it.', '2007-05-16 14:13:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(3656228, 508220, 50695, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>I don''t get any sense of an event from this photo, which probably explains your low score. The photo itself has an interesting composition, and I like the acid-washed earth tones. <br/> <br/>I do feel like it''s trying to tell me something, though, and I can''t figure out what it is. Your title is lost on me.</td>', 'Greetings from Critique Club  I don''t get any sense of an event from this photo, which probably explains your low score. The photo itself has an interesting composition, and I like the acid-washed earth tones.  I do feel like it''s trying to tell me something, though, and I can''t figure out what it is. Your title is lost on me.', '2007-05-16 14:25:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(3656258, 509485, 74588, '<td valign="top">unbelieveble that a bad postcard picc can get a blue ribbon   shame on you all</td>', 'unbelieveble that a bad postcard picc can get a blue ribbon   shame on you all', '2007-05-16 14:32:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3656278, 509369, 10867, '<td valign="top">What an amazing shot!  I''m not normally a fan of fisheye type shots, but in this case, the extreme wide angle has enabled you to show both the remarkable buildings surrounding the event and the huge skeleton and some of the "audience"!  If I''d voted in this challenge, I''d have given it the only 10 I''ve ever given!</td>', 'What an amazing shot!  I''m not normally a fan of fisheye type shots, but in this case, the extreme wide angle has enabled you to show both the remarkable buildings surrounding the event and the huge skeleton and some of the "audience"!  If I''d voted in this challenge, I''d have given it the only 10 I''ve ever given!', '2007-05-16 14:39:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(3656385, 509485, 29797, '<td valign="top">David, congratulations on your blue ribbon with such an OUTSTANDING photo! Into my favorites it goes!</td>', 'David, congratulations on your blue ribbon with such an OUTSTANDING photo! Into my favorites it goes!', '2007-05-16 15:16:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(3656530, 507555, 53572, '<td valign="top">a wonderful image, the super saturated colours and blown background work well here.  the expressions on the women''s faces are the perfect counterbalance to the heat of thier saris and the implied heat of the surroundings.<br/> <br/>i gave this a 9, and it was greatly underrated by the masses.  great work!</td>', 'a wonderful image, the super saturated colours and blown background work well here.  the expressions on the women''s faces are the perfect counterbalance to the heat of thier saris and the implied heat of the surroundings. i gave this a 9, and it was greatly underrated by the masses.  great work!', '2007-05-16 16:02:53.000000', NULL, 0),
